From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] binder_call_settings: take the MTK RIL's getCallWaiting
 response

VoiceCallWaiting never gets the real value on the Mindphone (MT6739), and
every query logs:

  Unexpected getCallWaiting response 31

radio::getCallWaitingResponse() in the vendor's librilfusion.so calls
vtable slot 0xac, which is getClirResponse, instead of 0xbc. The serial
and the error are right, and the two arguments are still the (enable,
serviceClass) that were meant for getCallWaitingResponse, so the
response is good as it is. The radio_client matches responses by serial,
so it can't be the reply to something else.

Take that response as well, for the HIDL interface, the only one which
the workaround is known to be needed for. Upstream dropped the check
altogether in aeb396b, which would hide other mixups here. Anything else
is still reported, and what comes with an error is still an error.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around a vendor RIL bug, upstream no longer checks the response code]
---
 src/binder_call_settings.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/binder_call_settings.c b/src/binder_call_settings.c
index 4011ba0..0c73bcf 100644
--- a/src/binder_call_settings.c
+++ b/src/binder_call_settings.c
@@ -186,6 +186,23 @@ binder_call_settings_cw_query_ok(
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * radio::getCallWaitingResponse() in librilfusion.so (MTK) calls the wrong
+ * vtable slot, so the result of getCallWaiting arrives as getClirResponse.
+ * The serial is the right one and the two arguments are the (enable,
+ * serviceClass) of getCallWaitingResponse, so it's what was asked for.
+ */
+static
+gboolean
+binder_call_settings_cw_resp_ok(
+    const BinderCallSettings* self,
+    guint32 resp)
+{
+    return (self->interface_aidl == RADIO_VOICE_INTERFACE) ?
+        (resp == RADIO_VOICE_RESP_GET_CALL_WAITING) :
+        (resp == RADIO_RESP_GET_CALL_WAITING || resp == RADIO_RESP_GET_CLIR);
+}
+
 static
 void
 binder_call_settings_cw_query_cb(
@@ -200,9 +217,7 @@ binder_call_settings_cw_query_cb(
     const BinderCallSettingsCbData* cbd = user_data;
 
     if (status == RADIO_TX_STATUS_OK) {
-        guint32 code = cbd->self->interface_aidl == RADIO_VOICE_INTERFACE ?
-            RADIO_VOICE_RESP_GET_CALL_WAITING : RADIO_RESP_GET_CALL_WAITING;
-        if (resp == code) {
+        if (binder_call_settings_cw_resp_ok(cbd->self, resp)) {
             if (error == RADIO_ERROR_NONE) {
                 if (binder_call_settings_cw_query_ok(cbd, args)) {
                     return;
